# Credentials for the integration checks. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.integrations.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored and is the ONLY place these belong. None of them is
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, so none reaches the browser or the deployed site — these are for
# scripts on this machine, not for the website.
#
# Nothing here is required. Every check reports "not set up yet" and carries on,
# so `npm run integrations:check` is useful before any of this is filled in.

# ── Google: Search Console + GA4, one service account ────────────────────
# Either the path to the downloaded key file, or the JSON itself on one line.
# A path is better: the key never enters a shell history or a process list.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=/Users/sharan/.config/gcloud/sharancreatedthis-seo.json

# The numeric property id from GA4 → Admin → Property details.
# NOT the G-XXXXXXXX measurement id, which is a different thing entirely.
GA4_PROPERTY_ID=

# How the property is registered in Search Console. A domain property verified
# by DNS is "sc-domain:example.com"; a URL-prefix property is the full URL.
GSC_SITE_URL=sc-domain:sharancreatedthis.in

# ── Microsoft Clarity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clarity → Settings → Data export → Generate new API token. Per project.
CLARITY_API_TOKEN=

# ── Bing Webmaster Tools ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bing Webmaster Tools → Settings → API access → API key.
# This key can SUBMIT URLs, not only read. Treat it as write-capable.
BING_WEBMASTER_API_KEY=

# ── Cloudflare ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. wrangler is already logged in and covers Pages and deployments;
# this is only needed for DNS and zone settings, which its OAuth scopes do not
# reach. Create at dash.cloudflare.com → My Profile → API Tokens → Custom:
#
#   Zone   → Zone      → Read     (zone: sharancreatedthis.in)
#   Zone   → DNS       → Read
#   Zone   → Zone WAF  → Read     (only if you want redirect rules listed)
#
# Deliberately all Read. Nothing in this repository writes DNS, and a token
# that cannot write is a token that cannot be turned against the domain.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# ── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to set. `gh` holds its token in the macOS keychain, which is better
# than any value in this file: encrypted at rest, and never in a file that can
# be copied, backed up or committed by accident.
